Description: A framework for the detection and redaction of personally
    identifiable data (PID) in free text via natural language processing (NLP).
    Provides a pipeline for tagging, reviewing, and redacting PID across
    collections of documents. The core tagger is built on 'UDPipe' models,
    with experimental support for 'spaCy' models (requires Python and the
    'reticulate' package) and a user-extensible interface for custom tagging
    engines. The main point of entry is the `pidpos()` function 
    (see `Trouble shooting the UDPipe Model` vignette for 
    possible issues with the automated downloading of the pretrained UDPipe 
    model).
